8-489c736ab489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668049} :answer-field/id #uuid "d72cfebc-159c-580f-999c-ca24781f79fd" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9392ab96-5be3-5aab-8c35-808d0b88162a" :question/math-academy-id "q-37384" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $1$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{18}=-3\\sqrt{2}$ is a not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\sqrt{6}$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $0$ is not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None of those listed\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8cd203b-0235-5547-88b9-dd0b5ff2c526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459921} {:answer/id #uuid "000e824e-f9f5-5ba7-9c14-3a48d73bd0fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8cd203b-0235-5547-88b9-dd0b5ff2c526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/v