7592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "016b340f-7aa5-5001-aeb3-927982c5cf50" :question/math-academy-id "q-104694" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $47$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{12}=-2\\sqrt{3}$ is not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\sqrt{10}$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $0$ is not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None of those listed\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124490 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca956d3e-37a8-5f0f-a062-97d0567d54e6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Bases of Abstract Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68307327-d553-5c0f-9277-b38e2b528f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461491} {:answer/id #uuid "78c1a89a-520f-55bb-aeb2-e65b35d1b2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68307327-d553-5c0f-9277-b38e2b528f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461491} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7e9756-5679-5939-b675-05db781b0860" :answer-field/key "$\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02422796-c8f7-540a-9e57-9f2c6bc52ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461493} {:answer/id #uuid "18fccc31-a4b6-5f00-aca3-c8da917759ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02422796-c8f7-540a-9e57-9f2c6bc52ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461493} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac1a6f96-76c2-548b-933c-7e9652bad3d7" :answer-field/key "$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "584b6ea8-930f-5b89-94ba-983ab55cd684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461495} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1bc6a2-d551-55b3-9121-200306d4de9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "584b6ea8-930f-5b89-94ba-983ab55cd684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461495} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec95b7a8-1630-5830-acd6-e28d5986273c" :answer-field/key "$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef0e7af-93b7-5531-809e-2739874c6809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667814} {:answer/id #uuid "98278eef-5c07-5da6-8278-6dd4517338a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98278eef-5c07-5da6-8278-6dd4517338a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667815} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0c1f94-476c-5bcb-83e5-4664ca8bd7dd" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fba7ca1e-918b-5610-87e4-9553b3a87d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107589" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$” is false. Since $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$, any vector of ${R}^{2},$ including the given vector $x,$ can be written as a linear combination of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ This means that $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$” is false. The set $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the vector ${b}_{3}$ is in ${R}^{3}$ but it is not a linear combination of  ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ as the set  $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent. This means that the set does not span ${R}^{3}$ and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$” is false. The set $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75270618-7af7-5381-9066-6d3469656acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461515} {:answer/id #uuid "67390882-204b-5352-ad1e-ccec65f496a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75270618-7af7-5381-9066-6d3469656acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461515} :answer-field/id #uuid "b208e569-82a8-5d09-9cd4-e626e88672d8" :answer-field/key "${y}^{2}{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}={y}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b1fb51-971c-5aa9-804d-0ccdfcc7a696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461517} {:answer/id #uuid "c7880ef3-333f-5868-b08a-8422f8cfd792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04b1fb51-971c-5aa9-804d-0ccdfcc7a696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461517} :answer-field/id #uuid "917fdd71-e52e-5156-b297-f58247d19d0f" :answer-field/key "$y{y}^{′}-x\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5587940f-b2d2-50f4-8efe-1abc1acf4aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461519} {:answer/id #uuid "41170317-0947-57dc-838f-57dc269df7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5587940f-b2d2-50f4-8efe-1abc1acf4aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461519} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ac02f9-35ab-51dd-af88-ea5627438f45" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c6fa98-1086-5078-afc2-610a6e78171a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667822} {:answer/id #uuid "9b99ccc6-dc62-536d-84bf-3cf54fe6f750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b99ccc6-dc62-536d-84bf-3cf54fe6f750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667823} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec80501f-be65-5cb6-b82a-55b8ce8f9653" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c444e682-8c21-501d-82e3-dbe63de4e200" :question/math-academy-id "q-108916" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{2}{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}={y}^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-x{y}^{3}={y}^{2}\n$$\n\nand this is not a Bernoulli differential equation because it is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{2}{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}={y}^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\n$$\n\nand this is not a Bernoulli differential equation because it is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x){y}^{n}$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given equations is a Bernoulli differential equation.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d454755c-f070-50aa-a288-101e2c21d000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461587} {:answer/id #uuid "30ee683c-53a6-59f7-8be2-89adc86a0928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d454755c-f070-50aa-a288-101e2c21d000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461587