0}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "815eec93-e015-5f93-a83b-b48b70c9e441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668720} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e8fe487-d986-550f-b434-f6b314bd80c1" :answer-field/key "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7fbfa1c-696c-569c-8a32-b9f903615eb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-80696" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{x({x}^{2}+1)}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{4x}{x({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+1=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4e358b5-97fa-5dc0-9ec4-19466342da0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469410} {:answer/id #uuid "6b93d7f8-3a76-5294-8c4b-a64beffd4684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4e358b5-97fa-5dc0-9ec4-19466342da0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469410} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a1473c4-f58e-5b7d-8f68-b11f5d273326" :answer-field/key "$3Q$ is orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041c92fd-b654-5bac-8d90-25928f746218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469412} {:answer/id #uuid "2d632d7e-d7b3-5411-87cd-979fb2168d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "041c92fd-b654-5bac-8d90-25928f746218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469412} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e09cf-386e-5aa7-97ec-f5672711e8a1" :answer-field/key "${Q}^{T}$ is **not** orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfb7808c-9349-508d-be48-6a448e81e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469414} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2826a9-8fd1-543d-8c80-03ed36d83923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfb7808c-9349-508d-be48-6a448e81e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469414} :answer-field/id #uuid "fefed51c-a546-5c98-b8b5-becce51ddb02" :answer-field/key "${Q}^{5}$ is the zero matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "927f8022-705c-5271-bda0-b8c3b10e7eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668725} {:answer/id #uuid "0644fcb8-b24d-52a8-9559-b1cc945aa919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0644fcb8-b24d-52a8-9559-b1cc945aa919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668726} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bc6a081-8853-5e38-a9f7-5d683643b1e4" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27c490dd-1808-531c-8cd0-cdd298d3c924" :question/math-academy-id "q-84786" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$3Q$ is orthogonal” is false. Computing the product $3Q\\cdot (3Q)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3Q\\cdot (3Q)^{T} & =3Q\\cdot 3{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =9Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =9I \\\\  & \\ne I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q}^{T}$ is **not** orthogonal” is false. Computing the product ${Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T} & ={Q}^{T}Q \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q}^{5}$ is the zero matrix” is false. Let's consider the identity matrix\n\n$$\nQ=I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that $Q$ is an orthogonal matrix and also ${Q}^{5}=Q\\ne O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157363 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5586c38-e0ca-5a6d-90ab-71c0fead2cc2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Point on a Solution Curve Is a Stationary Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1dca5fa-a9a7-5936-992b-453ceb07007e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469536} {:answer/id #uuid "dcce086a-9e68-5c53-8e57-74901b19c09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1dca5fa-a9a7-5936-992b-453ceb07007e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469536} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d55eb78-31a4-5821-8b16-c576014f0f3f" :answer-field/key "$(1,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e378b6-0af4-5188-a5e7-6414457f0464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469538} {:answer/id #uuid "82aee8a9-7717-5a7f-8a54-90dfa5eb69ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86e378b6-0af4-5188-a5e7-6414457f0464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469538} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e35b08f-b0c4-534c-9673-873356909333" :answer-field/key "$(2,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d6ac48f-d971-55cb-8b73-be946f446094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469540} {:answer/id #uuid "ad963729-b8c6-572d-b56a-b69a8f1b73af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d6ac48f-d971-55cb-8b73-be946f446094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469540} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cac8d36-0d1c-5fa4-a1fa-2903f72a8f08" :answer-field/key "$(e,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d680240-1d25-5843-87f4-ef89dcf7284f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668729} {:answer/id #uuid "69dd8594-8e27-56d1-af07-de4791aa95d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69dd8594-8e27-56d1-af07-de4791aa95d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668730} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5df78a-5f99-5a9a-8fd8-e29a243a8125" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e87b95d9-4b1d-5eb0-8c89-8d155a899eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-89871" :question/problem "Consider the solution curves of the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{′}={e}^{y}.$ Which of the following points are stationary points of their respective solution curve?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stationary point of $y(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $y$ such that ${y}^{′}(c)=0.$ \n\nFirst, we make ${y}^{′}$ the subject of the equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{′}={e}^{y}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{′}=\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of our points into the differential equation and calculate the value of the derivative: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{y}^{′}|}_{(1,0)} & ={\\left(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}}\\right)|}_{(1,0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0}}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ {{y}^{′}|}_{(2,-2)} & ={\\left(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}}\\right)|}_{(2,-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2}}{(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2}}{4} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ {{y}^{′}|}_{(e,1)} & ={\\left(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}}\\right)|}_{(e,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{1}}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the points are the stationary points of the function.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f901a3ab-3b58-51a1-b653-f88ac4b09060" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Second Derivative Test To Classify a Point on a Solution Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d03fa37-ca1a-54f9-a3eb-5a8bf1effac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469548} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc192d1-a596-57f1-9e52-7df28aa3631a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d03fa37-ca1a-54f9-a3eb-5a8bf1effac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469548} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7d22a00-7d6c-5c4f-863f-4b796b7ee608" :answer-field/key "$(\\pi ,1)$ is a stationary point of the function $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85798085-cefc-5be0-8526-fcbe0d58d21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469550} {:answer/id #uuid "468e2470-d7f7-5d4e-92ac-43fe7a8570ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85798085-cefc-5be0-8526-fcbe0d58d21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469550} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b85f1f5-9e6e-5497-98df-d403ecceb824" :answer-field/key "$(\\pi ,1)$ is a local maximum point of the function $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb0b04ec-3384-54b7-bdeb-6b2b7ad2fe88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469552} {:answer/id #uuid "5188a600-1360-5a9d-9060-fbdd68ab3467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb0b04ec-3384-54b7-bdeb-6b2b7ad2fe88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469552} :answer-field/id #uuid "51d29dc4-cdf3-5410-965e-98b9294f009d" :answer-field/key "$(\\pi ,1)$ is an inflection point of the function $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acdab16b-82d5-51aa-a2d5-79fae210b5fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668731} {:answer/id #uuid "0cbedbe3-3676-5e87-8482-ff0c5fa59989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cbedbe3-3676-5e87-8482-ff0c5fa59989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668732} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8b00336-c0c0-570d-b881-57b371691c99" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1e244cae-49ac-5727-b109-5857ab506f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-89887" :question/problem "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGiven that the point $(\\pi ,1)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x),$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the first and second derivatives of the function at the given point.\n\nTo find the first derivative of $f$ at $(\\pi ,1),$ we substitute the coordinates of our point into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\pi ,1)} & ={(y+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)|}_{(\\pi ,1)} \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the second derivative, we first need to differentiate the equation and then substitute the coordinates of the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =(y+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =y+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(\\pi ,1)} & ={(y+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)|}_{(\\pi ,1)} \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =1+0-2 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$(\\pi ,1)$ is a stationary point of the function $f$” is false. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\pi ,1)}=1\\ne 0,\n$$\n\nwe obtain that $(\\pi ,1)$ is not a stationary point of the function $f.$\n\n- Statement “$(\\pi ,1)$ is a local maximum point of the function $f$” is false. There is no critical point at $(\\pi ,1),$ therefore we cannot have a local maximum at that point.\n\n- Statement “$(\\pi ,1)$ is an inflection point of the function $f$” is false. Since the second derivative is not zero, there is no inflection point at $(\\pi ,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aedcb32b-f84c-5aa2-b3a4-f7e83746b836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468882} {:answer/id #uuid "aed73398-59c2-51b4-9371-f0f65e98014f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aedcb32b-f84c-5aa2-b3a4-f7e83746b836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468882} :answer-field/id #uuid "9958dde5-b255-5d95-ae9b-baca80f743d5" :answer-field/key "$v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3915fd0e-f480-5ebd-983a-af8001f5e607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468884} {:answer/id #uuid "23790615-5ac5-5c45-97e2-001e01eff0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3915fd0e-f480-5ebd-983a-af8001f5e607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468884} :answer-field/id #uuid "03f1a276-3cb9-581b-9099-1990fdc1c513" :answer-field/key "$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a54f6205-db26-5c00-8932-ebcca124f521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468886} {:answer/id #uuid "40b5715b-352e-56b1-a124-d548af347d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a54f6205-db26-5c00-8932-ebcca124f521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468886} :answer-field/id #uuid "1659548f-da18-5fc1-9233-0906388e6725" :answer-field/key "$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b24a61-77ec-5f5c-a385-6d6495ede91e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668987} {:answer/id #uuid "9e9c36be-507e-53b7-abfd-ca9b1b1cb137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e9c36be-507e-53b7-abfd-ca9b1b1cb137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668988} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9a1127-88a3-5c02-9b63-9e94e83f7e19" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "83c9089c-246d-51fb-b493-4538acc22376" :question/math-academy-id "q-109574" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A+I:$\n\n$$\nA+I=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A+I:$\n\n$$\n(A+I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+I:$\n\n$$\n(A+I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A+I:$\n\n$$\n(A+I)x=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{v}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e12609b7-286b-50a8-8373-a331d60ab904" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4e29d4-8ab4-51b2-bed7-3d933724288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469038} {:answer/id #uuid "366b643d-0477-56b8-99e8-05665c95ecc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e4e29d4-8ab4-51b2-bed7-3d933724288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469038} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa806480-98e3-5de9-ac37-45bb7e60daee" :answer-field/key "If $\\text{Ker}(T)={⟨x,y,z⟩\\,|\\,x+y=0}$ then $\\text{rank}(T)+1=n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dba33dd-efd6-5edd-8cb4-431f80150830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469040} {:answer/id #uuid "03dbdbf2-dd97-5434-bd34-a6b20449669a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dba33dd-efd6-5edd-8cb4-431f80150830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469040} :answer-field/id #uuid "bad0d392-5687-58fc-8043-83455bbb6881" :answer-field/key "If there exists a vector $v\\notin \\text{Im}(T),$ then $|T|\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c5c5fde-9d69-5dd0-bd3e-c686ea921e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469042} {:answer/id #uuid "c12380e7-7519-5b6e-8745-f0b879e1df9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c5c5fde-9d69-5dd0-bd3e-c686ea921e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469042} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9fc1cb-34d2-5ac7-b925-bd6d7335fddb" :answer-field/key "If ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent and $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})=0$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae2fdb5d-d681-5e12-86b2-43a446a00c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669187} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb93cfb-f3d9-566e-86a2-a7e90b6a6203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bb93cfb-f3d9-566e-86a2-a7e90b6a6203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669188} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa60747f-d618-56ee-8f14-ab31df27e310" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "936f721f-93be-5c51-8233-7da49b500101" :question/math-academy-id "q-38979" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{n}$ into ${R}^{n},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\left\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}\\right.$ \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “If $\\text{Ker}(T)={⟨x,y,z⟩\\,|\\,x+y=0}$ then $\\text{rank}(T)+1=n$” is false. Solving $x+y=0$ for $x,$ we get $x=-y.$ Therefore, any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-y \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=y\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{v}_{1}}+z\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{v}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}.$ Therefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=2.$ Finally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(T)+2 & =n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “If there exists a vector $v\\notin \\text{Im}(T),$ then $|T|\\ne 0$” is false. If $v\\notin \\text{Im}(T)$ then $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{n}$, so, according to the invertible matrix theorem, $T$ is not a bijection. Thus, the matrix $T$ is not invertible, and, consequently, $|T|=0.$\n\n- Statement “If ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent and $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})=0$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$” is false. Since $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})=0$, then ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T).$ But the vectors are linearly independent, therefore, the dimension of  $\\text{Ker}(T)$ is at least $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b65968b-6028-551a-9631-58b67db16afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469374} {:answer/id #uuid "a75e0f1b-240f-5f97-b88c-017b10166d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b65968b-6028-551a-9631-58b67db16afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469374} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7a2f7a7-5e01-577f-9f82-f523dd836563" :answer-field/key "$2PQ$ is always orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8af276a-607f-58cb-95a3-dfb795f49d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469376} {:answer/id #uuid "de04d0f8-5260-5b89-a3cd-b666a82c85fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8af276a-607f-58cb-95a3-dfb795f49d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469376} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d01531c-c3a3-5572-8137-9d105c60ab89" :answer-field/key "$P-Q$ is always orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470300} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0feb765d-c901-5436-a1e5-1524e2608115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469378} {:answer/id #uuid "aadde301-7372-5694-8cca-d9b6c7b72bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0feb765d-c901-5436-a1e5-1524e2608115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469378} :answer-field/id #uuid "e169f11f-de5b-5f0d-ad57-d18c3a6c238d" :answer-field/key "$P$ is **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100da194-a562-5cf8-bac5-2f2795e39f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669233} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c88d4b-3026-5253-8242-d5bb96261dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3c88d4b-3026-5253-8242-d5bb96261dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669234} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c74a023-89da-5a1c-9a41-47e0a1c5dddb" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e6401598-f82b-58db-b408-23496dde6519" :question/math-academy-id "q-84344" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrices $P$ and $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$2PQ$ is always orthogonal” is false. Computing the product $(2PQ)\\cdot (2PQ)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2PQ)\\cdot (2PQ)^{T} & =2PQ\\cdot 2{Q}^{T}{P}^{T} \\\\  & =4P(Q{Q}^{T}){P}^{T} \\\\  & =4P(I){P}^{T} \\\\  & =4I \\\\  & \\ne I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P-Q$ is always orthogonal” is false. As a counterexample, consider the following subtraction of two orthogonal matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe resulting matrix is not orthogonal since, for example, its first column is not normalized.\n\n- Statement “$P$ is **not** invertible” is false. The inverse of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is given by ${P}^{-1}={P}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ccf9fe-9fff-57a9-9304-9ed3ab411a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470949} {:answer/id #uuid "cd38aae3-eb89-502e-95f5-f0b67c9bface" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ccf9fe-9fff-57a9-9304-9ed3ab411a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470949} :answer-field/id #uuid "b676af05-3dc2-57c5-937a-36acc27a6987" :answer-field/key "$F$ is **not** conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d25790-233a-5252-8654-1ee93a945a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470951} {:answer/id #uuid "88bef363-90dd-5f58-8f3e-0e6fa9a731c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4d25790-233a-5252-8654-1ee93a945a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470951} :answer-field/id #uuid "b508976c-ce23-5a0b-8ee8-1332aba82f50" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f1634ca-676c-56be-805f-f8a4da6ba9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470953} {:answer/id #uuid "2d74d261-31ed-592a-8886-2e31a70f20d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f1634ca-676c-56be-805f-f8a4da6ba9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470953} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a1e2d7d-bec5-5fe7-8248-ae4746a2c58c" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9710463e-4d66-5de0-aa7f-2a13fd536838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669005} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc574f6-f2de-5cb2-80df-71c62786fab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fc574f6-f2de-5cb2-80df-71c62786fab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669006} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a7b498e-8ca9-58dc-9151-1230bcc40ace" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d4a2162-ef8c-55f6-9a59-3237823f3b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125660" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({e}^{x+y}-4x)\\,i+({e}^{x+y}+6y)\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is **not** conservative” is false. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement “${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2067362d-b2dd-5b81-a0c0-254679d504c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470973} {:answer/id #uuid "85d673ae-d427-529a-a86e-84c5f3aca678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2067362d-b2dd-5b81-a0c0-254679d504c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470973} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d2487c1-305d-5d73-b58d-603c12dd9b35" :answer-field/key "$c=-1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf13b53-53c5-595b-b162-9c02134b389f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470975} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4fee56-e3c7-5fe0-b2bf-af7d6065e33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf13b53-53c5-595b-b162-9c02134b389f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470975} :answer-field/id #uuid "6697dd78-1361-5fb4-a196-6b0e79a6e315" :answer-field/key "$c=0$ gives the $y$-axis, excluding the origin" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9766d54-18d4-55a2-a11d-25dda37f5384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470977} {:answer/id #uuid "e67bade9-f7b9-51f8-8efc-a33eb81a712c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9766d54-18d4-55a2-a11d-25dda37f5384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470977} :answer-field/id #uuid "7014990a-205c-5f78-a1f4-b40b21737c3d" :answer-field/key "$c=1$ gives the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab14c2a6-a598-5ac5-839a-eebd57d6f315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669021} {:answer/id #uuid "189f0029-79a2-5c16-a9a2-6a0b0264c926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "189f0029-79a2-5c16-a9a2-6a0b0264c926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669022} :answer-field/id #uuid "69eb2f7b-dfda-55c8-813d-ba545e514a58" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac11e3e9-cb1c-5541-98a0-caa6e8b5b278" :question/math-academy-id "q-129059" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{x} & =c \\\\ x+y & =cx \\\\ y & =(c-1)x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is the line $y=-2x,$ excluding the origin. So, “$c=-1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin” is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=-x,$ excluding the origin. So, “$c=0$ gives the $y$-axis, excluding the origin” is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, “$c=1$ gives the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin” is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83796fe8-f045-5dbc-94d1-6d6e031f3ed8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Line Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12dfb173-85de-53de-8bbb-769e3ff393b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471059} {:answer/id #uuid "dee9be9f-4d3b-54bb-b16b-61cd95251fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12dfb173-85de-53de-8bbb-769e3ff393b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471059} :answer-field/id #uuid "98f7413f-d2af-5cef-8961-04ae15531969" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472035} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5daac8d8-5f6f-5451-86d9-365c0f6282a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471061} {:answer/id #uuid "c23b81bd-b600-5fba-9034-aa425ea45b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5daac8d8-5f6f-5451-86d9-365c0f6282a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471061} :answer-field/id #uuid "359f2089-4bbe-5fdf-a7c3-8c747afc5255" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69b3e9f5-b9e7-5b2c-b9df-8010d612b348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471063} {:answer/id #uuid "68ee5432-10cb-51f0-885c-08f97a2fa22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b3e9f5-b9e7-5b2c-b9df-8010d612b348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471063} :answer-field/id #uuid "659695e3-c6ca-568b-aa80-eef126aeff96" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71fc54c9-49f4-50e5-81f0-4f589a575427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471065} {:answer/id #uuid "feb87bed-8997-5d53-80a5-8aa6ed79649d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71fc54c9-49f4-50e5-81f0-4f589a575427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471065} :answer-field/id #uuid "c353328a-e322-53ed-a610-69474e8dc78a" :answer-field/key "$L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da1b9df2-38a6-5fd5-9f82-71fb8868eba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669065} {:answer/id #uuid "60b0ab00-84df-5694-93f1-c369a6c1f92c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60b0ab00-84df-5694-93f1-c369a6c1f92c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669066} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dad2842-2277-5719-8125-6b02e11446a0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55724e97-d014-5bc4-825e-d54d7bbd24c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-157462" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in ${R}^{3}$ that passes through the points $(0,-1,2)$ and $(1,2,0).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is false.The direction vector of the line $L$ is \n\n$$\nd=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{y+1}{3}=\\frac{z-2}{-2}.\n$$\n\nBut this line does not pass through the origin since \n\n$$\n(0)\\ne \\frac{(0)+1}{3}\\ne \\frac{(0)-2}{-2}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L$ (the position vectors of the given points). Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the point $(1,1,2)$ does not belong to $L$ since\n\n$$\n(1)\\ne \\frac{(1)+1}{3}\\ne \\frac{(2)-2}{-2}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is false. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3018fd-9d16-578f-b050-966890844c9b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Plane Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c937576f-6d5f-55a1-8ab7-74336373ddca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471067} {:answer/id #uuid "47583555-84d1-5a39-b1b9-e6047a8944af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c937576f-6d5f-55a1-8ab7-74336373ddca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471067} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab90d14-b0ba-5a9b-855f-b992a23b0955" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2ee9f06-9f88-5319-ab23-eafad8031298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471069} {:answer/id #uuid "32c5a5bd-0cd6-58b3-8aca-cdd9c3ba44f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2ee9f06-9f88-5319-ab23-eafad8031298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471069} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0460439-3543-5a2d-8246-30fddc3afbca" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e8c45b4-79e9-59f1-8aed-0fe57c1e774f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471071} {:answer/id #uuid "7b261e97-d4f1-5864-8cd7-0b630c489dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e8c45b4-79e9-59f1-8aed-0fe57c1e774f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471071} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e759f3-3ea4-52e5-91d5-d81ad7bd1e88" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a389ed-2a90-5310-9d49-d9de078d0e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471073} {:answer/id #uuid "14b87aa4-7616-54b5-993b-17ac7bcfc6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34a389ed-2a90-5310-9d49-d9de078d0e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471073} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bac6d2b-71be-5d31-8a9c-1f6b199802d9" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c734eefe-de11-5133-a634-625ab193030d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669067} {:answer/id #uuid "0a5f9e72-fc00-57ea-bd06-6f3e9150a5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a5f9e72-fc00-57ea-bd06-6f3e9150a5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669068} :answer-field/id #uuid "34f2ba81-0efa-5ed3-88f6-8ca5344a19d1" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7a73387-34bf-50c1-bd13-d6c9025be3b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-157470" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $2x-y+z=2$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ 2-2x+y\\end{bmatrix},\\,x,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The line does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z & =2 \\\\ 2(0)-(0)+(0) & =2 \\\\ 0 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0+0 \\\\ 0+(-2) \\\\ 2+0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $Π$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z & =2 \\\\ 2(0)-(-2)+(2) & =2 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin Π,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is false. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3018fd-9d16-578f-b050-966890844c9b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Plane Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "700557ce-6572-5ee2-a07f-34d93423cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471075} {:answer/id #uuid "c353aaf6-90db-54f4-992e-599b27b80250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "700557ce-6572-5ee2-a07f-34d93423cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471075} :answer-field/id #uuid "334fdb1c-33a5-5fc3-a6c1-ca14b6176b0d" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1b9382-ab0d-51d1-b161-c5849bc1195f" :answer/type {:db/id