ct {:answer/id #uuid "85d0b485-371d-58e9-a8c2-75e1166ae969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471081} :answer-field/id #uuid "894f59eb-e3c4-5a32-80d8-8b6c6c7a4fbb" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5e17d59-24d8-531f-b766-175aa0e1a548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669069} {:answer/id #uuid "69dd6996-2e74-57f7-9133-267f2b058768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69dd6996-2e74-57f7-9133-267f2b058768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669070} :answer-field/id #uuid "720265f4-c654-586c-8444-ad99c2584d53" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6fdf40e-16e2-5d4d-87e5-0c2a5c46b067" :question/math-academy-id "q-157475" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $3x+2y+z=1$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ 1-3x-2y\\end{bmatrix},\\,x,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The line does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z & =1 \\\\ 3(0)+2(0)+(0) & =1 \\\\ 0 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0+1 \\\\ 0+(-1) \\\\ 1+0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $Π$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z & =1 \\\\ 3(1)+2(-1)+(1) & =1 \\\\ 2 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin Π,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is false. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84280041-92fd-5192-93c9-e48627a8d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470703} {:answer/id #u