id "3380502f-56f6-501e-b560-ed1186ab069f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82324" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{2}-1,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. For instance, $f(-1)=0=f(1)$, but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors When the Denominator Has Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c2e0a46-a4ee-5819-bfd8-b6605a0d8094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439879} {:answer/id #uuid "e9369708-bcb2-5c13-a3f7-152ce020d3b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c2e0a46-a4ee-5819-bfd8-b6605a0d8094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439879} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3d5ff2-3ae3-55